-- =============================================================================
-- Eden Apothecary: pre-1900 energetics sources for 25 more herbs (research
-- batch 6). DATA ONLY. Written 2026-09-15.
-- =============================================================================
-- Approved by the founder on 2026-09-15, as researched.
--
-- Writes public.herbs.energetics_citation for 25 herbs that had NULL
-- (8 where the old sources agree, 4 where they disagree and the page says so,
-- 6 with no pre-1900 source found at all). Same jsonb shape as batches 1 to 5,
-- carrying 'batch': 6.
--
-- This batch DOES change app values: 10 readings on 7 herbs, each one approved
-- by the founder individually. A value may only move where the STORED value is
-- unclear, which here means the record hedges itself, and where named counted
-- first-hand sources support the new reading. A clear stored value is never
-- touched. Section 3 asserts that EXACTLY these moved and nothing else did.
--
--   H077 Betony (Wood), temperature:
--     'Warm (mildly)'
--       -> 'Warm'
--   H086 Catnip, temperature:
--     'Warm (warming diaphoretic, paradoxically calming)'
--       -> 'Warm'
--   H086 Catnip, moisture:
--     'Slightly drying'
--       -> 'Dry'
--   H087 Coltsfoot, temperature:
--     'Neutral to slightly warm'
--       -> 'Warm'
--   H087 Coltsfoot, moisture:
--     'Moistening (demulcent)'
--       -> 'Dry'
--   H088 Comfrey, temperature:
--     'Cool to neutral'
--       -> 'Cool'
--   H088 Comfrey, moisture:
--     'Moistening (demulcent)'
--       -> 'Moist'
--   H093 Elecampane, moisture:
--     'Slightly drying'
--       -> 'Dry'
--   H095 Fenugreek, moisture:
--     'Moistening (mucilaginous when soaked)'
--       -> 'Dry'
--   H098 Ground Ivy, temperature:
--     'Warm (slightly)'
--       -> 'Warm'
--
-- Every UPDATE is guarded on the exact value read live from production on the
-- day this file was generated, and RAISEs rather than write if the live value
-- no longer matches. A re-run where the value is already corrected is a no-op
-- with a notice.
--
-- 7 herbs here found old readings but counted none of them (wrong species,
-- wrong plant part, a group statement, or the writer quoting someone else).
-- Each carries its own plain sentence saying why, free to read, per the founder
-- decision of 2026-09-15 that silence on such a page reads as 'nobody looked':
--   H076 Arnica:
--     'No pre-1900 source found for this exact plant. The old books that carry the name Leopard's bane are describing Doronicum, a different genus, and the one chapter that may be this plant cannot be pinned to it.'
--   H079 Black Walnut:
--     'No pre-1900 source found for this exact plant and part. The one old reading is for the European walnut, and it describes the kernel rather than the hull, leaf and bark.'
--   H082 Blue Vervain:
--     'No pre-1900 source found for this exact plant. Every old reading describes the European vervain or the Chinese ma bian cao, not the North American blue vervain this entry is about.'
--   H084 Boswellia:
--     'No pre-1900 source found for this exact plant and part. Frankincense is a traded resin that several Boswellia trees make, and the old books either describe that shop drug or describe the tree rather than its resin.'
--   H085 Bugleweed:
--     'No pre-1900 source found for this reading. The one old writer only supposes it, and the other says plainly that nobody before him had written anything about the plant's qualities.'
--   H089 Corn Silk:
--     'No pre-1900 source found for this part. The one old reading describes the grain, and this entry is about the silk.'
--   H100 Bacopa (Brahmi):
--     'No pre-1900 source found for this exact plant. The Sanskrit brahmi of the old dictionaries is a different plant, and the writers who do describe this one give no temperature or moisture.'
--
-- BLAST RADIUS: production data on 25 of 300 herbs in public.herbs, one column,
-- energetics_citation, on rows where it is currently NULL. No temperature or
-- moisture changes, no schema change, no view change, no grant change, no RLS
-- change. The 69 legacy single-source citations and the 125 herbs already carrying
-- a batch object are untouched.
--
-- IDEMPOTENT. Verification aborts the whole transaction on any failure.
-- =============================================================================

begin;

